'''wood-end''' (wu̇d′end), ''n.'' Same as ''hood-end.''

'''wood-engraver''' (wu̇d′en-grā″vėr), ''n.'' '''1.''' An artist who engraves on wood.—'''2.''' In ''entom.'', any
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Wood-engraver (''Xyleborus cælatus''), eight times natural size.}}}}
one of several bark-beetles of the genus ''Xyleborus'' and allied genera; specifically, ''X. cælatus.'' {{smaller|This works in the cambium layer of pine-trees in the United States in such a way that, on removing the loosened bark, the surface of the wood is seen furrowed in a regular and artistic manner, numerous galleries passing off at right angles from a straight median tunnel.}}

